    "text": "<p>Two simple harmonic motion, are represented by the equations</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>cos</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Ratio of amplitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is</p>"
